  "details": "This is a bug report and a feature request. The new nameplate system completely trashes group banners, which didn't have a great standard (or any standard, for that matter), to begin with.\n\nCurrently, on live, a (mostly) consistent group banner means uploading a mostly transparent picture with the actual banner in the middle. This is wasting tons of space that could be actually used to show other art or graphics on the group page.\n\nThe image scales very poorly on some parts of the site, as well.\n\n- Our uploaded group banner is 2000x1126, following this ***unofficial*** guide: https://www.reddit.com/r/VRchat/comments/10e11hb/groups_banner_guide/\n\n- The [main group page](https://vrchat.com/home/group/grp_638f485d-f83d-4ae2-a559-63bcacb1faba) shows the original 2000x1126.\n\n- A [group event page with no custom thumbnail](https://vrchat.com/home/group/grp_638f485d-f83d-4ae2-a559-63bcacb1faba/calendar/cal_fa8e4eef-4b43-4323-99cc-9cb1e28d8210) 1024x576\n\n- The [groups landing page](https://vrchat.com/home/groups) scales the image to 256x144. This is extremely bad if you have made a banner with transparency, as per above.\n\n- I'm sure there are many more exposed within the client itself and maybe other parts of the website. But I think this is a good demonstration of how wildly inconsistent this group feature is.\n\nAnd now on beta with the new nameplate, we see just a few pixels of the group banner. This is effectively useless now for representing a visual of your group. I've attached a picture showing some of these inconsistencies.",
